WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is
the White House corresponden

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.736 size:75% position:38% line:92%
for "PBS News Hour."

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Yamiche Alcindor.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.806 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How are you, Yamiche?

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.909
-I'm doing well in this new life
that we're living.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.711 line:92%
-We are actually used to -

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should say I'm used to
seeing you out.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm used to seeing you at
White House press conferences.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is nice to also
see you inside.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:24.024
How has this been, going t
White House press conference

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.025 size:81% position:41% line:92%
during this situation?

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.194 size:81% position:41%
-It's been incredibly,
incredibly sobering.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is, of course,
a scary and wild time.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:35.568
So every day as I leave
my house, I'm putting on a mask.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.236 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I'm wiping my hands.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.205
And I'm also, of course,
balancing the normal things I do

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
every day, which is making sur
I know what questions

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to ask and what sources
I want to check in with.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:47.380
So it just seems like there'
this added level of seriousnes

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.116
and craziness to what was
already a sort of crazy

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.652
political time I would say
in the last three years.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:56.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, of course, one thing
a journalist doesn't want to d

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.923 line:92%
is become part of the story.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.325
You've been put in a awkward
situation whereas you've asked

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:03.229
very fair questions that the
President has framed as nasty.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:06.633
He's told you to be nice
and to not be threatening.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is going through your min
in those moments

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you realize
you are a part of this story

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to just
getting the story?

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:17.310
-What's going through my mind is
that I became a reporter

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.680
because I think everyday people,
vulnerable populations,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
deserve a voice,
especially at the White House.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
So as the President may be
lashing out at me

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
and other reporters,
the thing I keep thinking is

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.189 line:92%
"Okay, but people need answers

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.525
We're in this time where peopl
want to know, 'Can I get a test?

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
Am I going to be
able to survive?

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.362
How's my family going to d
when we're losing our jobs?'

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think all of those thing
come to my mind.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in my own mind
think of myself

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a civil rights reporter
so a lot of times

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm thinking about
all the different people

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've met over my career
on the streets

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
and on different stories
and thinking they need answers

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.311
They want me to remain
professional and focus on

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
why I came to
the White House today.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to compliment you
for the fact

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you keep your poise
in those moments.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't believe
I would be able to do so.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.187 line:92%
When you get home, do you vent

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:04.324
Is there a time that you get out
those moments?

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm lucky because I got
married about two years ag

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:11.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I run home to this cute bo
that lives with me

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I decompress with
my husband.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.167 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I talk about my day.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.303
But I also do things like listen
to Bill Withers on repeat

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.740
and remember that there are so
many better days ahead of us

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.811
and that everyone should kind of
decompress and calm down.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.914
So I personally really tak
the time to dance around

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.150
my apartment and to just talk to
my husband.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's the way
that I've had to --

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.620
that's the way I've been able to
weather all of this.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think a lot of us
have found that we're luck

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:40.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have families in times like
this to create a cushion

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the moment
we are going through.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you just speak -- you know
because obviously,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.565 line:92%
you've been covering this stor

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.300 size:75% position:38%
like your colleagues
from the beginning.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.770
Can you speak to what you
believe the root causes ar

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.938 line:92%
for not just how this started --

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
and no one thinks it's the
current administration's fault

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
this virus exists --

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
but their failures
to sort of deal with it.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
What the root causes
of that were?

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think there were two
really big things going on

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.287 line:92%
The first is that the President,

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
before this coronavirus
outbreak,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was making government
smaller in his mind.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:16.462
And in that regard he disbande
the National Security Council'

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
office that
deals with pandemics.

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
He also really pared down
the CDC's staff.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:25.638
So there was one moment where --
or one thought

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.108
that the President was reall
making sure the government

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.810 size:88% position:44% line:92%
was smaller in his mind.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other thing that was
going on, though,

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.314
that was President Trump
was downplaying the virus.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:38.151
He was telling reporters like me
and signaling to Americans

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:41.087 size:84% position:42%
all over the country
that this was something

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:41.888 line:92%
that wasn't that serious,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it was going to
be gone by April,

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this was going to be
some sort of miracle

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was gonna
just be washed away.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:50.530
And because of that, you had
those two things come together

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now that's why you hav
a lot of people

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
criticizing the President'
response,

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, one, they didn't seem
to be ready for a pandemic

00:03:56.369 --> 00:04:00.106
and, two, the President, onc
a pandemic was on his doorstep

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was downplaying it,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.176 size:78% position:39%
thinking really about
his political future

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:03.843 size:75% position:38% line:92%
in a lot of regards,

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.312 size:88% position:44%
and thinking about being
re-elected as President.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the strange things
that we've seen

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
as these press conferences
get longer

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you have a situation
not just that the Presiden

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
will contradict himself
day to day,

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
he sometimes
will contradict himself

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
within the body of
an hour-long press conference.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:21.894
Is it refreshing, then, to hav
someone like Dr. Anthony Fauci

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the dais
who's a bit more consistent?

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is it true
that you have spoken to hi

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.500 size:81% position:41% line:92%
directly through this?

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have spoken to Anthony Fauc
directly.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:33.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a day where there wa
some stories about him

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
being excluded
from the White House briefings

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:35.908 line:92%
so I contacted his office,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.778
and he actually called me back
which was pretty surprising.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.214
And the first time he called m
back I didn't pick up the phon

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.116 size:88% position:44%
because I thought he was
literally a prankster.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I eventually
called him back.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.687 size:84% position:42%
And of course his voice
is very, very distinct,

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.388 size:78% position:39% line:92%
so I knew it was him.

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was stressing to me
that his relationship

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the President
is really good

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that he's focused on doing
the work of the people.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.562
I think it's refreshing in som
people's minds to, of course

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
have scientists who are expert
to talk about this.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is, of course,
the fact that the Presiden

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.802 line:92%
constantly contradicts himself

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:06.005
And that's why as a reporter
I often ask the President,

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:09.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Look, you said this
but you are now saying this.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:09.842 size:88% position:44% line:92%
How do you square that?"

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
The President sometimes
gets mad at that.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.446
But I think it's doing a service
to people to be able

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:16.549
to point out every single day,
as much as you possibly can,

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the President
often not only shares

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.554 size:88% position:44%
misleading information
but contradicts himself,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.588 line:92%
sometimes within minutes.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned you're
a civil rights reporter.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.025 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That's where you began.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are the sort of storie
you cover.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been seeing more and mor
in recent weeks

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:33.533
that this is disproportionally
affecting minority communities

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:36.369
Is there -- Do you have
any optimism or any sense

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:39.038
that there's a plan within
the White House to address that?

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.574
-As of now they're signaling
that they don't have a plan.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.677
But it's also because they don't
actually have the data

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.411 size:81% position:41% line:92%
to even create a plan.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:49.382
Lawmakers have been pushing fo
federal data to be collected

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.616 line:92%
and then shared when it comes to

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
looking at
the racial disparities.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:55.188
We know that black people
in most cities and states

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.055 line:92%
around the country are dying

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.358 size:81% position:41%
because they have more
underlying conditions

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.093 line:92%
like asthma and diabetes.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
And part of that is systemic
racism and the conditions

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
that African-Americans
often live in this country

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:08.601
But I think that there isn't a
this point a particular plan

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.570 size:78% position:39%
And Dr. Anthony Fauci
talked about this.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said
they're collecting the dat

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
and once they have
information to share,

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll be able to
share more about that.

